<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105900" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυμπᾰν-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>beat a drum,</i> as was done in the worship of
			Cybele, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				77
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.60a
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τυμπανίζεσθαι κατὰ τὰς ἐξόδους</span>”
				<i>march out to the sound of drums,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					15.1.58
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ἐπὶ ταῖς θύραις</span>
			<i>drum with the hand</i> on them, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>1 Ki.</u>
				21.13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> perh. 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποτυμπανίζω</span>
			 (which is v.l.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Hebr.</u>
				11.35
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			); coupled with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνασκολοπίζεσθαι</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>JTr.</u>
				19
			</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τύμπανον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> of orators,
			'beat the big drum', <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VS</u>
				1.21.5
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
